From 80ed862389656b234f1f8c175ecc077c15bce5fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:01:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Contain step-loop faults and publish only the in-flight
 request

- A throw in the step loop no longer escapes the synchronous path
  (IntegratedEndTimeCore) into Coordinator.Tick, where it stopped every
  held order releasing each tick; the shot declines and is warned once
  per ammunition. A worker catches per request and completes it as a
  decline instead of stranding its key for 10 s.
- _inFlight maps each key to the request it waits on, and DrainCompleted
  publishes only that request, so an older request finishing after an
  eviction and re-queue can no longer overwrite the fresh answer.
- The stranded-key timer counts solve time once a worker has taken the
  request (10 s) and queue time before that (60 s), so a backlog on a
  slow machine is not evicted as a dead worker.
- A declined or implausible worker result runs only the tiers below the
  integrator (LowerTiers), not a second full integration on the main
  thread.
- Worker results are cached with their capture time as origin, so
  TryCached reports the geometry's real age.
- EstimateForDisplay uses a firing-cache hit when there is one and runs
  at most two real solves per frame, keeping the last value for rows
  over budget, instead of one integration per row inside OnGUI.
- InterceptTime is read with Convert.ToSingle rather than unboxed.
- WorkerFaults and WorkerAborts reset per mission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
